#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Uburyo"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Mode which cacti will attempt to authenticate against the LDAP server.<blockquote><i>No Searching</i> - No Distinguished Name (DN) searching occurs, just attempt to bind with the provided Distinguished Name (DN) format.<br><br><i>Anonymous Searching</i> - Attempts to search for username against LDAP directory via anonymous binding to locate the user's Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>Specific Searching</i> - Attempts search for username against LDAP directory via Specific Distinguished Name (DN) and Specific Password for binding to locate the user's Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>One-Time Passwords (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti binds the user's password only once, during final authentication.  <i>No Searching</i> performs no directory lookup and binds directly using the Distinguished Name (DN) template, so it is safe for OTP when the DN template alone identifies the user.  When a directory lookup is required to resolve the DN, use <i>Specific Searching</i> with a dedicated service account (or <i>Anonymous Searching</i> where the directory permits it) so the lookup never consumes the user's single-use code.  For resilient OTP deployments use a single DNS load balancer name in the Server(s) field rather than a space delimited multi-server list, which would re-attempt the bind with an already-consumed one-time password."
msgstr "Uburyo Cacti izagerageza kwemeza umwirondoro kuri seriveri ya LDAP.<blockquote><i>Nta gushakisha</i> - Nta gushakisha Izina Ritandukanya (DN) kubaho, ahubwo igerageza guhuza ikoresheje imiterere y'Izina Ritandukanya (DN) yatanzwe.<br><br><i>Gushakisha mu buryo butazwi</i> - Igerageza gushakisha izina ry'ukoresha mu bubiko bwa LDAP binyuze mu guhuza mu buryo butazwi kugira ngo ibone Izina Ritandukanya (DN) ry'ukoresha.<br><br><i>Gushakisha mu buryo bwihariye</i> - Igerageza gushakisha izina ry'ukoresha mu bubiko bwa LDAP ikoresheje Izina Ritandukanya (DN) ryihariye n'Ijambobanga ryihariye mu guhuza kugira ngo ibone Izina Ritandukanya (DN) ry'ukoresha.<br><br><i>Amagambobanga akoreshwa rimwe (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti ihuza ijambobanga ry'ukoresha rimwe gusa, mu gihe cyo kwemeza umwirondoro bwa nyuma.  <i>Nta gushakisha</i> ntishakisha mu bubiko kandi ihuza mu buryo butaziguye ikoresheje inyandikorugero y'Izina Ritandukanya (DN), bityo ikaba yizewe kuri OTP igihe inyandikorugero ya DN yonyine igaragaza ukoresha.  Iyo gushakisha mu bubiko bikenewe kugira ngo DN iboneke, koresha <i>Gushakisha mu buryo bwihariye</i> hamwe na konti ya serivisi yabigenewe (cyangwa <i>Gushakisha mu buryo butazwi</i> aho ububiko bubyemera) kugira ngo ishakisha ritigera rikoresha kode y'ukoresha ikoreshwa rimwe.  Kugira ngo imikoreshereze ya OTP yihanganire ibibazo, koresha izina rimwe rya DNS load balancer mu mwanya wa Server(s) aho gukoresha urutonde rwa seriveri nyinshi zitandukanyijwe n'umwanya, ibyo byakongera kugerageza guhuza hakoreshejwe ijambobanga rikoreshwa rimwe ryamaze gukoreshwa."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Izina Rihariwe (DN)"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "The \"Distinguished Name\" syntax, applicable for both OpenLDAP and Windows AD configurations, offers flexibility in defining user identity. For OpenLDAP, the format follows this structure: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD provides an alternative syntax: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, commonly known as \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". In this context, \"&lt;username&gt;\" represents the specific username provided during the login prompt. This is particularly pertinent when operating in \"No Searching\" mode, or \"Require Group Membership\" enabled."
msgstr "Imyandikire ya \"Izina Rihariwe (DN)\", ikoreshwa ku igenamiterere rya OpenLDAP na Windows AD, itanga uburyo bworoshye bwo gusobanura umwirondoro w'umukoresha. Kuri OpenLDAP, imiterere ikurikiza iyi nyubako: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD itanga indi myandikire: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, izwi cyane nka \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". Muri ubu buryo, \"&lt;username&gt;\" ihagarariye izina ry'umukoresha ryihariye ryatanzwe mu gihe cyo kwinjira. Ibi ni ingenzi cyane igihe hakoreshwa uburyo bwa \"Nta Shakisha\", cyangwa iyo \"Gusaba Kuba mu Itsinda\" bishobojwe."

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Require Group Membership"
msgstr "Bisaba kuba mu itsinda"

#: include/global_settings.php user_domains.php
msgid "Require user to be member of group to authenticate. Group settings must be set for this to work, enabling without proper group settings will cause authentication failure."
msgstr "Bisaba ko ukoresha aba ari mu itsinda kugira ngo yemezwe umwirondoro. Igenamiterere ry'itsinda rigomba kuba rishyizweho kugira ngo ibi bikore; kubikoresha nta genamiterere rikwiye ry'itsinda bizatera ikibazo cyo kutemezwa kw'umwirondoro."

